---
code: whylog-absent
when-fires: `dorc why --last` was asked to replay the last run but no durable exists in the whylog directory (no prior run wrote one, or the wrong directory). cli --last reader.
why: the durable is written only when a plan/apply/round-trip run was asked to (spike: the `--whylog-dir` opt-in; product: quietly beside its work); a `--last` with nothing to replay is a benign no-answer, not a crash. Pull-surface: Warning, Floor::None. `{dir}` = the whylog directory searched. Remediation register (help) wanted: run a plan/apply first (or point --whylog-dir at the right directory) to produce a durable to replay.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- whylog-absent && mise run loom:promote -- whylog-absent`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all whylog-absent` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc why --last --whylog=.whylog
whylog: warning[whylog-absent]: there is no saved why-log in `.whylog` to read
back
   = help:  a why-log is saved when a plan or apply runs with `--whylog-dir`;
            run one first, or point `--whylog-dir` at the right directory

$ dorc-loom vars --used whylog-absent
case: whylog-absent
{{dir}} = ".whylog"
